Apply a monitor rule's vrr when the config is reloaded

Comparing a monitor rule with the active one ignored vrr, so a rule that
changed only vrr counted as unchanged and the active rule kept the old value.
And a config reload runs ensureVRR before the deferred monitor-rule pass has
updated the active rule, so even a rule that did change took effect only on
the reload after. Turning VRR on for a monitor took a mode change and two
reloads, or a new session.

Count vrr as a soft difference, and run ensureVRR for every monitor the
deferred pass refreshed.

Not yet upstream.

--- a/src/config/shared/monitor/MonitorRule.cpp
+++ b/src/config/shared/monitor/MonitorRule.cpp
@@ -26,8 +26,9 @@
     const auto SAME_AUTO_DIR  = m_autoDir == other.m_autoDir;
     const auto SAME_RESERVED  = m_reservedArea == other.m_reservedArea;
     const auto SAME_MIRROR    = m_mirrorOf == other.m_mirrorOf;
+    const auto SAME_VRR       = m_vrr == other.m_vrr;
 
-    if (!SAME_CM || !SAME_POS || !SAME_TRANSFORM || !SAME_AUTO_DIR || !SAME_RESERVED || !SAME_MIRROR)
+    if (!SAME_CM || !SAME_POS || !SAME_TRANSFORM || !SAME_AUTO_DIR || !SAME_RESERVED || !SAME_MIRROR || !SAME_VRR)
         return COMPARISON_SOFT_MISMATCH;
 
     return COMPARISON_FULL_MATCH;
--- a/src/config/shared/monitor/MonitorRuleManager.cpp
+++ b/src/config/shared/monitor/MonitorRuleManager.cpp
@@ -187,6 +187,13 @@
             m->m_activeMonitorRule.m_disabled ? m->onDisconnect() : m->onConnect(true);
     }
 
+    // a rule's vrr only takes effect through ensureVRR, which a config reload runs
+    // before this deferred apply has updated the active rule
+    for (const auto& m : monsForRefresh) {
+        if (m->m_output && m->m_enabled)
+            ensureVRR(m);
+    }
+
     for (auto const& w : Desktop::windowState()->windows()) {
         w->updateSurfaceScaleTransformDetails();
     }
